Virginia/North Carolina) across 26 three-year primary periods (1938-2014), compiled from collection records; years within a period are secondary occasions and the number of collections per HUC-year is the effort covariate.","reference":"Frimpong, E. (2017). Fish Detection Histories and Covariates, Upper and Middle New River Drainage Basin (Virginia and North Carolina, USA). Harvard Dataverse, V1.","short":"New River fish records"},{"table":"galvez_2021_araucania_comm","description":"Camera-trap detection/non-detection of guigna, Molina's hog-nosed skunk, foxes (Lycalopex), domestic dog and domestic cat at 180 grid-cell camera stations over up to 14 five-night occasions in agricultural landscapes of La Araucania, Chile (2019), with camera nights and human detections per occasion and 13 landscape metrics per station.","reference":"Galvez, N., Infante, J., Fernandez, A., Diaz, J., & Petracca, L. (2021). Land use intensification coupled with free-roaming dogs as potential defaunation drivers of mesocarnivores in agricultural landscapes. Journal of Applied Ecology, 58(12), 2962-2974.","short":"Araucanía camera traps"},{"table":"hamer_2024_hungary_amph_comm","description":"Detection/non-detection of nine amphibian species (eggs, larvae or adults) at 100 ponds in Hungary over three combined visual/dip-net/trap surveys in 2023, with eight per-survey covariates (date, VES effort, water temperature and level, wind, rain, fish, emergent vegetation).","reference":"Hamer, A. J., & Horanyi, J. (2024). Improving inference within freshwater community studies: Accounting for variable detection rates of amphibians and fish. Ecology and Evolution, 14(10), e70383.","short":"Hungarian pond amphibians"},{"table":"kery_2005_mallard_count","description":"Mallard counts on up to 3 surveys of 239 Swiss MHB 1-km2 quadrats (235 surveyed), with standardised elevation, transect length, forest, survey intensity and date (unmarked::mallard; Kery, Royle & Schmid 2005).","reference":"Kery, M., Royle, J. A. & Schmid, H. (2005). Modeling avian abundance from replicated counts using binomial mixture models. Ecological Applications 15(4), 1450-1461.","short":"Swiss MHB mallard (counts to 0/1)"},{"table":"kery_2008_willowtit_occ","description":"Willow tit detection/non-detection on 3 surveys of 237 Swiss MHB 1-km2 quadrats, with standardised elevation, forest, transect length, survey date and intensity (unmarked widewt.csv; the dataset of the unmarked overview vignette and AHM1 ch. 10).","reference":"Fiske, I. & Chandler, R. (2011). unmarked: An R package for fitting hierarchical models of wildlife occurrence and abundance. Journal of Statistical Software 43(10).","short":"Swiss MHB willow tit"},{"table":"kery_2010_crossbill_dynocc","description":"European crossbill detection/non-detection on up to 3 surveys per year, 1999-2007, at 267 Swiss MHB 1-km2 quadrats, with elevation, forest cover and survey date (unmarked::crossbill; the colext vignette and AHM2 ch. 4 dataset).","reference":"Fiske, I. & Chandler, R. (2011). unmarked: An R package for fitting hierarchical models of wildlife occurrence and abundance. Journal of Statistical Software 43(10).","short":"Swiss MHB crossbill"},{"table":"kery_2014_mhb_comm","description":"Counts of 158 bird species on up to 3 surveys of 267 Swiss MHB 1-km2 quadrats in 2014, with quadrat coordinates (unspecified CRS), elevation, route length, forest, survey date and duration, observer and species traits (AHMbook::MHB2014; the AHM1 ch. 11 community dataset).","reference":"Kery, M. & Royle, J. A. (2016). Applied Hierarchical Modeling in Ecology, vol. 1. Academic Press. Ch. 11.","short":"Swiss MHB 2014 community (counts to 0/1)"},{"table":"malhotra_2021_loslagos_comm","description":"Camera-trap detection/non-detection of chilla fox, culpeo fox, guigna and domestic dog at 48 camera stations over up to 12 seven-day occasions in a fragmented agricultural landscape of Los Lagos, Chile (2019), with six camera-level habitat covariates.","reference":"Malhotra, R., Jimenez, J., & Harris, N. (2021). Patch characteristics and domestic dogs differentially affect carnivore space use in fragmented landscapes in southern Chile. Diversity and Distributions, 27(12).","short":"Los Lagos camera traps"},{"table":"schank_2015_tapir_occ","description":"Daily camera-trap detection/non-detection of Baird's tapir at 22 cameras (6-72 camera-days each) in Rio Indio, Nicaragua, June-August 2014, with camera-days of effort and coarsened (0.1 degree) camera coordinates.","reference":"Schank, C. (2015). Tapir detection histories (Tapirus bairdii) from Rio Indio, Nicaragua [Data set]. Zenodo.","short":"Nicaragua tapir cameras"},{"table":"smith_2019_greatbasin_csf_edna","description":"Sample-level eDNA detection (0/1, any of three qPCR replicates) of the Columbia spotted frog in three filter samples at each of 168 sites nested in 61 Great Basin watersheds (Oregon, Idaho, Nevada), 2015-2016, with site and watershed covariates; the authors' multi-scale occupancy input. First eDNA / multi-scale table.","reference":"Smith, M. M., & Goldberg, C. S. (2020). Occupancy in dynamic systems: accounting for multiple scales and false positives using environmental DNA to inform monitoring. Ecography, 43(3), 376-386.","short":"Great Basin frog eDNA (filter samples)"},{"table":"smith_2019_greatbasin_csf_qpcr","description":"qPCR-replicate detections (0/1; 3 replicates x 3 filter samples) of Columbia spotted frog eDNA at 168 Great Basin sites, 2015-2016, with the site-level visual/dipnet confirmation as a covariate; the authors' false-positive occupancy input. Companion to smith_2019_greatbasin_csf_edna.","reference":"Smith, M. M., & Goldberg, C. S. (2020). Occupancy in dynamic systems: accounting for multiple scales and false positives using environmental DNA to inform monitoring. Ecography, 43(3), 376-386.","short":"Great Basin frog eDNA (qPCR replicates)"},{"table":"tleimat_2023_ecuador_capuchin_occ","description":"Camera-trap detection/non-detection of Ecuadorian capuchins at 21 stations over 39 two-week intervals (Dec 2019 - Jun 2021) in Ecuador, with 19 station-level habitat covariates; no coordinates.","reference":"Tleimat, J., McCracken, S. F., Lynch, R., Rodriguez, D. & Fritts, S. (2023). Capuchin Detection History [Data set]. figshare.","short":"Ecuador capuchin cameras"}]}
